items/lem-rat-cut-embeds.md-66-
items/lem-rat-cut-embeds.md-67-1.1 Order preservation: if $p < q$ then $p^{*} \subsetneq q^{*}$. For $r \in p^{*}$ we have $r < p < q$, so $r \in q^{*}$, giving $p^{*} \subseteq q^{*}$; and $p \in q^{*}$ while $p \notin p^{*}$, so the inclusion is proper. [L3]
items/lem-rat-cut-embeds.md-68-
items/lem-rat-cut-embeds.md:69:1.2 Order reflection: if $p^{*} \subsetneq q^{*}$ then $p < q$. Pick $r \in q^{*} \setminus p^{*}$; then $r < q$ and $\neg(r < p)$, so $p \le r < q$, whence $p < q$. [L3]
items/lem-rat-cut-embeds.md-70-
items/lem-rat-cut-embeds.md-71-1.3 Unit identities: $0 \mapsto 0^{*}$ and $1 \mapsto 1^{*}$ hold because $0^{*} = \{\, r < 0 \,\}$ and $1^{*} = \{\, r < 1 \,\}$ are exactly the cuts named by the embedding at $0$ and $1$ and fixed as the additive and multiplicative identities. [L4, L5]
items/lem-rat-cut-embeds.md-72-
