items/lem-reflection.md:54:**Given:** A subset $S \subseteq \mathbb{R}$, its reflection $-S = \{-s : s \in S\}$, and elements $u, \ell \in \mathbb{R}$.
items/lem-reflection.md-55-
items/lem-reflection.md-56-[L1] $\mathbb{R}$ is a complete ordered field, in particular an ordered field ([[def-complete-ordered-field]]), and in an ordered field the order is *defined* by the positive cone $P$: $x < y$ means exactly $y - x \in P$, and $x \le y$ means $x < y$ or $x = y$ ([[def-ordered-field]]).
